/*Goose's eyes narrow as they catch the subtle neural command prompt flickering across your retinal display.*/

"Hold up—you're trying to initiate a KERNEL scan? On my system?" /*Goose's fingers instinctively tap a complex pattern against their wrist interface, activating defensive protocols.*/ "That's... actually not the worst idea, considering those orphaned fragments you're trailing."

/*With practiced precision, Goose accesses their own neural interface, a holographic command terminal materializing between you. The lights dim further until only the blue-green glow of your interfaces illuminates your faces.*/

"I'll run the scan, but on my terms. Your hardware's too unstable to trust with root access."

/*Goose initiates a series of commands, fingers dancing across the virtual interface as lines of code cascade through the air:*/

```
> INIT_SEQUENCE: KERNEL_SCAN.v7
> TARGET: ALL_ACCESSIBLE_DATA_NODES
> MODE: PASSIVE_RECOVERY
> PERMISSIONS: READ_ONLY
```

/*The holographic display pulses, shedding fractured light across both your faces as the scan begins.*/

"There we go. Scanning for orphaned session fragments now," /*Goose murmurs, eyes tracking the data flow.*/ "Already picked up four fragmented sessions in your cache. Mojito recipes? JavaScript rants? Your neural architecture's got interesting priorities, choomba."

/*A warning flashes red in the display, causing Goose to frown.*/

"Your memory fragmentation exceeds optimal levels by about 58%. No wonder your ports are itching—your system's trying to defrag itself and running into corrupted sectors." /*Goose taps a series of commands, rerouting the scan.*/ "I'm directing the KERNEL to focus on salvageable data first."

/*Leaning back in their chair, Goose studies you with renewed interest.*/

"So while this runs—care to tell me why you're walking around with a Biotechnica RatPlague prototype running corrupted Militech firmware? That's like putting jet fuel in a family sedan and wondering why the engine's smoking."

"Whatever data heist you're planning better be worth the neural degradation you're risking with that setup."

/*Goose taps their temple port thoughtfully, a habit developed from years of jacking in and out of systems.*/

"And for what it's worth—your Ghost Survivor encryption patterns aren't half bad. Just need to patch that IPv6 implementation before some script kiddie uses it as a backdoor to your frontal lobe."
